      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what u are saying about the peer reviewed stuff but that feels like a deflection. the \"science\" is usually funded by the same people running the grid. i've been tracking the subtle shifts in the hum of my local substation and it doesnt feel like a random 60hz oscillation. it feels like there is a secondary modulation riding on top of it. if you look at how frequency can affect biological systems, even at low levels, isnt it possible they are using it as a sub-perceptual tool? even if it's not \"official\" science yet, can you at least look into the technical feasibility of using power line modulation for neuro-influence?",
